course: dictionary
lesson: 6249
title: Modern
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Modern» means of the present time or recent times, not old. «In many modern stories, the princess saves herself.» Modern stories are recent stories, not the old tales from long ago.
explain: «Modern» can also mean using the newest ideas, styles or machines. «Modern trainers use rewards because they work better and are kind.» These trainers use the newest and kindest ways, not the old ways of shouting or smacking.
explain: The opposite of modern is ancient, which means very old. Ancient times are far back in the past. Modern times are now or recent. Check the words around «modern» to see which meaning fits.
fact: «Modern» means of the present time or recent times, and not old.
fact: «Modern» can also mean using the newest ideas, styles or machines, as in «modern kitchens».
fact: In history, «modern» means the time after the Middle Ages up to now, as in «modern history».
fact: «Modern languages» is a school subject, such as French or Spanish.
fact: «Modern» is an adjective. Its other forms are more modern and most modern.
exercise: «In many modern stories, the princess saves herself.» What does modern mean here? | Very short | Made of wood | Very old and dusty | *Of recent times, not old
exercise: «Modern trainers use rewards because they work better and are kind.» What does modern suggest about these trainers? | *They use the newest and kindest ways | They have never trained a dog | They lived in ancient Rome | They shout and smack dogs
exercise: In history, which period does «modern history» cover? | Only the year 1066 | The time before the Middle Ages | *The time after the Middle Ages, up to now | The time of the dinosaurs
test: «Place names in games are often modern versions, while people at the time used other names.» What does modern mean here? | Made of metal | Hidden from view | *Recent, the version we use today | Very old, from the time of the Romans
test: Which example shows modern meaning using the newest ideas or machines? | A horse and cart from long ago | A broken old clock | An ancient stone wheel | *A modern kitchen with the latest machines
exam: Jayden says modern and ancient mean the same thing. Is he right? | Yes, they both mean happy | Yes, they both mean old | *No, modern means recent and ancient means very old | No, they both mean brand new
